        "proof_or_evidence": "No full proof; the convex-order/coupling tool is structurally OBSTRUCTED and I pin down exactly why. (a) g is not convex and means differ, so convex order is out (as the prompt noted). (b) Usual stochastic dominance fails because dilations c*consec give identical L_y but reshuffle the p-vector, so no distribution can dominate all competitors — verified 0/N hold. (c) The decisive obstruction: L_y=sum y_r S_r has ALTERNATING-sign y_r. A per-moment domination proof (S_r(E)<=S_r(consec) for y_r>0 and >= for y_r<0) is impossible because consec is NOT extremal on the positive-weight moments: at k=8 the y_2>0 moment S_2 is beaten by 32 competitors, and the y_4>0 S_4 / y_0 S_0 are consec-max, while the negative-weight S_1,S_3 are consec-MIN (consistent with minimizing a negatively-weighted term) — but S_1 min FAILS for some E too. So L_y maximality is a genuinely NON-SEPARABLE cancellation across moments, confirming the prompt's non-separability fact independently. (d) Naive coupling 'compress E toward consec by single decrements never decreases p_0' is FALSE: explicit counterexamples e.g. k=8 (0,1,2,3,4,5,7,13) has p_0=0.1785 but its decrement (0,1,2,3,4,5,7,12) has p_0=0.0840 (number-theoretic resonance spikes at spread 12,13), and k=9 (0..6,12) p_0=0.3718 > (0..6,11) p_0=0.3354. This re-confirms the DEAD ROUTE 'local monotone descent / gap-contraction (kps-S8)' now directly at the p_0 level. POSITIVE residue: p_0=sum_r (-1)^r S_r (true incl-excl over the 6 inner sectors, reconstructed exactly), and consec strictly maximizes p_0 — a cleaner, fully exact lemma than L_y maximality and a better proof target. Scripts: 04-computation/lrc14_angleA_convex_order.py, lrc14_angleA_ties_and_order.py, lrc14_angleA_p0_and_S1.py, lrc14_angleA_p0_proof_probe.py, lrc14_angleA_sector_symmetry.py; outputs in 05-knowledge/results/lrc14_angleA_*.out.",
        "remaining_gap": "No proof that consec maximizes p_0 or L_y at general/infinite spread. The coupling/convex-order family of tools is now shown to be the WRONG hammer (alternating moment signs => no separable/monotone-order argument can work; dilation invariance => no stochastic-dominance argument can work). What is needed instead: either (i) a direct argument that consec strictly maximizes p_0=meas{x: all 6 inner sectors hit} via the structure of the AP orbit {frac(jx): j=0..k-1} as a single arc-of-arcs cover (three-gap/Steinhaus theorem governs the AP orbit's gap structure and is the natural remaining lever, NOT yet exploited), or (ii) accept p_0-maximality as the target (cleaner than L_y) and prove it; note L_y>=p_0 with extra nonneg terms, so p_0-maximality alone does NOT give L_y-maximality — the alternating tail (1/10)p_3+p_6 (k=8) resp. (5/18)p_1+(1/9)p_4+(1/6)p_5 (k=9) must still be controlled jointly. The non-separability is intrinsic, so any proof must handle the signed cancellation directly rather than bounding moments one at a time.",
