          "evidence": "Independently reverified every quantitative claim with my own Fractions breakpoint engine and own moment/finite-difference code (scripts: C:\\Users\\Eliott\\Documents\\GitHub\\math\\04-computation\\lrc14_verify_angleA_independent.py and lrc14_verify_angleA_part2.py).\n\nEXACT MATCHES (to the digit):\n- consec values: k=8 p_0=481/1470=0.327211, L_y=2633/7350=0.358231; k=9 p_0=2447/5880=0.416156, L_y=26083/52920=0.492876.\n- y_r weights: independently inverted g(t)=sum_r y_r C(t,r) by finite differences -> k=8 y=[1,-1,1,-9/10,3/5,0,0], signs alternate (+,-,+,-,+) exactly as claimed; verified sum y_r S_r = L_y and g(t)=sum y_r C(t,r) for all t.\n- incl-excl identity p_0 = sum_r (-1)^r S_r reconstructs p_0 exactly (both k).\n- palindrome J[j]=J[6-j] for consec exact (k=8 J[1]=J[5]=799/2940, J[2]=J[4]=179/735).\n- (d) decrement counterexamples exact: k=8 (0,1,2,3,4,5,7,13) p_0=1137/6370=0.17849 -> decrement p_0=247/2940=0.08401; k=9 {0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,12} p_0=0.3718 -> {...,11} p_0=0.3354. Monotone-descent/gap-contraction genuinely fails at p_0 level.\n\nMAXIMIZER claim (1)(2) reproduced AND stress-tested harder than claimed: consec strictly maximizes BOTH L_y and p_0 with ZERO beats and ZERO non-dilation ties over primitive sets at k=8 maxval<=14 (3431 sets), k=9 maxval<=13 (1287), k=10 maxval<=13 (715) — and survives a wider stress test k=8 maxval<=18 (31788 primitive sets, 0 beats on both).\n\nBASIS logic validated: S_1 NOT minimized by consec (1 competitor strictly smaller, k=8), refuting 'AP most equidistributed'; S_2 (positive y-weight) beaten by 32 competitors, confirming the non-separable cancellation that blocks per-moment domination; g non-convex with differing means rules out convex order.\n\nMINOR PRESENTATIONAL CAVEATS (not refutations): (i) claim says usual stochastic dominance holds for 0/3430 at k=8 — I count 1, because consec trivially dominates itself; the substantive 'no COMPETITOR dominates' is correct. (ii) The k=9 counterexample