          "evidence": "Reproduced every exact claim with an independent Fraction-based breakpoint engine (04-computation/verify_angleD_kps.py, verify_angleD_kps2.py; outputs in 05-knowledge/results/verify_angleD_kps.out, verify_angleD_kps2.out).\n\n(1) consec distributions EXACT MATCH, all sum to 1:\n  k=8: [481/1470,359/1470,25/147,26/245,17/210,5/98,1/49], p0=481/1470=0.327211\n  k=9: [2447/5880,653/2940,27/196,23/245,13/196,9/196,1/56], p0=2447/5880=0.416156\n  k=10:[8899/17640,551/2940,127/1176,145/1764,55/882,5/126,1/63], p0=8899/17640=0.504478\n  Confirms the prompt's stated p0 values and confirms the correction: the guessed 2402/7350(=0.32680) is WRONG; correct k=9 p0 is 2447/5880=0.416156.\n\n(2) Dilated AP {0,2,...,2(k-1)} has IDENTICAL full distribution to consec at k=8,9,10 (not just equal L_y) — confirmed, consistent with THM-531 scale-invariance.\n\n(3) consec UNIQUELY maximizes p0=meas(S7) over bounded-spread valid E: k=8 spread<=11, 330 gcd=1 sets, 0 beat and 0 tie (the AP class only ties when {0,d,...,7d} fits the window; AP {0,2,...,14} ties consec p0 exactly = 481/1470).\n\n(4) maxgap<1/7 => N=0 verified POINTWISE (0 violations at all 126/154/196 breakpoint-midpoint intervals for k=8/9/10), and meas{maxgap<1/7} = 44/735, 47/294, 11/49 (exact match), all < p0 — so three-gap multiset is sufficient but not necessary, confirmed.\n\nNEGATIVE results confirmed:\n(a) No pointwise coupling: N_consec(x) > N_E(x) on 30-36 intervals per competitor (k=8: 30-31; k=9: 32-36) — within the claimed 30-98 range; kills naive pointwise domination.\n(b) No FOSD: consec fails to be tail(P(N>=t))-dominated for 329/330 competitors (k=8) and 44/45 (k=9) — i.e. all-but-one, matching the claimed 119/120 and 44/45 (the all-but-one structure is robust; only the k=8 denominator differs due to a wider spread window, qualitative conclusion identical).\n\nCAVEAT: This is the claimed VERIFIED-FACTS bundle, all of which hold exactly. It does NOT prove the crux HYP-2607 (consec maximizes L_y over ALL valid E) — the negative results (a),(b) explicitly show the extremality is signed and not explained by any monotone/stochastic-order coupling, consistent with canon. The verdict CONFIRMED applies to the stated facts and negative results, not to a proof of HYP-2607."
